# --- generated / regenerable ---------------------------------------------
# _raw_ids.json is 17 MB of intermediate data produced by
# _probe/semantic/extract_ids.py from the shipped .dat in ~5 s.  It is an input
# to build_semantic.py, never a source: committing it would make every clone
# carry a copy of the game's data.
_probe/semantic/_raw_ids.json
_probe/semantic/_unresolved_ids.json
_probe/semantic/_tech_diag.json
_probe/schema/AGE3NamesV0007.json
_probe/schema/age_label_tables_raw.json

# The AGE source tree is extracted from the game's own
# Tools_Builds/docs/Source.7z.  It is third-party source under GPLv3/LGPLv3,
# it is 2.4 MB of C++, and it is reproducible from the installed game:
#   tar -xf "<game>/Tools_Builds/docs/Source.7z" -C _probe/source
# Keeping it out of the repo keeps the licence question out of the repo too.
_probe/source/
aoe2docs/

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc

# --- outputs --------------------------------------------------------------
_probe/out_*/
_probe/out_*.txt
_probe/out_*.err
# `Start-Process -RedirectStandardError` writes this pair; naming it after the
# commit the run describes is the only way to tell two runs apart afterwards.
_probe/err_*.txt
发布包/
_shots/
*.zip
*.7z

# --- what the 2026-10-25 cleanup deleted (10.7 GB -> 476 MB) -----------------
# Sweep frames from live-game rounds: 356 entries, 8.0 GB.  The verdicts live in
# `_probe/report_*.md` and `_交接说明.md`; the six frames worth looking at are copied to
# `_evidence/`, whose README says what each one proves.
_probe/shots/

# Build outputs: 120 dirs, 1.6 GB.  `_probe/out_*/` above covers the `out_` spelling;
# these are the `_box_out` / `_group_out` / `*_out` ones.  Nothing tracked lives inside and
# each is rewritten by the suite that names it, so deleting them costs one re-run.
_probe/*_out/

# A stray directory written by a python that is not this project's runtime.
_probe/ident/

# --- kept evidence ----------------------------------------------------------
# `_evidence/README.md` is tracked and says what each picture proves; the pictures are
# 5 MB full-screen grabs, so they stay out of the repository.
_evidence/*.png
_evidence/*.jpg

# --- scratch --------------------------------------------------------------
_probe/tmp_*.py
_probe/tmp_*.ps1
_probe/tmp_*.txt
# Recon probes dump their findings as JSON next to themselves (tmp_recon3.json,
# tmp_wall.json, ...).  The same convention: a scratch answer, not a source.
_probe/tmp_*.json
#
# A snapshot of the player's own mod list, taken before an experiment touches it, and
# a log of what went to the recycle bin.  Both are records -- `tmp_objrepl_restore.py`
# reads the first to put the profile back -- and both are about this machine, not the
# project.
_probe/objrepl_snapshot.json
_probe/recycle_list.txt
_probe/_newlog.md
# Written every run by _probe/schema/test_branch_extract.py: a human-readable
# PREVIEW of what the branch extractor saw.  The artifacts that matter are the
# checked-in tables beside it (attribute_labels.json etc.), generated by
# build_schema.py after someone has read this preview.  Committing it would make
# a scratch dump look like a source of truth.
_probe/schema/regen_preview.json

# --- team audit artifacts --------------------------------------------------
# Each auditor teammate copies its own aoe2mod tree and dozens of 11.4 MB .dat
# scratch copies; keep only their REPORT.md, never the scratch/mutation forests.
_probe/team/*/scratch/
_probe/team/*/mutations/
_probe/team/*/__pycache__/

# The artifact emitter's scratch: 11.4 MB of .dat per run, regenerable by
# _probe/datparse/emit_mod.py (which verify_artifact.py then checks).
_probe/datparse/out_modtest/

# _probe/verify_agevariant_artifact.py's scratch mod (11.9 MB .dat).  Note the
# pattern above (_probe/out_*/) does NOT cover a directory named just out.
_probe/out/

# _probe/test_sld_encode.py writes a repainted .sld here (703 KB, regenerable).
_probe/_sld_out/

# The UI shell's default output: one 12 MB .dat per build.  Regenerable from the
# screen or from `_probe/test_ui_server.py`, and never something to commit.
_mods_out/

# _probe/test_new_unit_box.py builds real mods to re-read the emitted .dat: one
# 12 MB .dat per assertion that touches the file.  Regenerable in ~20 s.
_probe/_box_out/
# Contact sheets the icon probes draw (probe_icon_sheet.py,
# probe_material_index.py).  Regenerable from the installed game in
# seconds; committing them would put the game's own artwork in the repo.
_probe/asset_index/png/

# --- looking at the game's own screen -------------------------------------
# The screen channel: every frame grabs a 1900x1000 client area (about 4 MB as
# PNG) and one hover sweep leaves 40-120 of them behind.  They are evidence for
# one measurement, not sources: the scripts that take them are committed, the
# pixels are re-takeable in seconds, and a handful of sweeps would otherwise be
# larger than every line of code in this repo.
_probe/shots/
_probe/*.png
# The player's own screenshots, kept here by hand so the agent can OCR them.
截图/
# Probes that write a small JSON answer beside themselves.  The answer is the
# conclusion and belongs in the docs; the file is one run's output.
_probe/play_last.json
_probe/w1_last.json
_probe/bisect_results.json
_probe/btn_hits.json
_probe/v23_facts.json
# Screen tools that were measured and did NOT work, kept out of the tree so a
# later session does not reach for them again:
#   hovergrid.ps1  hovers with SetCursorPos, which emits no movement event, so
#                  the game never learns the cursor moved (0 changed pixels
#                  measured against 3491 for SendInput).  sendgrid.ps1 replaces it.
#   ocr_screen.ps1 WinRT OCR: reads 4-5 lines out of the in-match HUD where
#                  tmp_rapidocr.py reads 17-68.  Kept as a note, not a tool.
#   click_at.ps1   first click attempt, no hover first; gamescreen.ps1 supersedes it.
_probe/hovergrid.ps1
_probe/ocr_screen.ps1
_probe/click_at.ps1

# Screens the screen-reading probes leave behind: one measurement each, useful for
# a minute and then stale.  Same rule as the frames above -- evidence, not sources.
_probe/card_last.json
_probe/nomod_last.json
_probe/queue_scan.json
_probe/objreplacement_abba.json

# Build output of the probes that run the real emitter (test_linked_group.py and
# tmp_tg_bundle.py).  Regenerated on every run; a mod folder checked in would drift
# from the code that produced it.
_probe/_group_out/
_probe/out_tg/
_probe/out_tg_bundle/

# Backups of the game's own files taken while testing in-place edits.  They are
# copies of shipped data, so they stay out of the tree; the restore step and the
# sha256 comparison are in the reports beside them.
_probe/backup_objreplacement.json
_probe/shipped_objreplacement_backup.json

